WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.950
Let’s do a range check with real numbers.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.075
Follow it on screen.

3
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.100
The chart shows the range line as zero four two, true.

4
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.025
Variation is six degrees west.

5
00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:17.725
We’re going from true toward magnetic, which is uncorrecting, so we add west.

6
00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:21.800
Zero four two plus six is zero four eight, magnetic.

7
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.350
You line up on the range, and your compass reads zero five one.

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.825
The compass reads three degrees more than magnetic.

9
00:00:30.075 --> 00:00:32.850
So is the deviation east or west?

10
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.175
Compass best, error west.

11
00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:38.325
Three degrees west.

12
00:00:38.575 --> 00:00:41.675
Write it on your deviation card for that heading.

13
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:43.850
That’s lesson ten.

14
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.200
Heading is where you point, track is where you go.

15
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.975
Relative bearings start at the bow.

16
00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:53.350
And a range is the best compass check there is.

17
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.000
Next time: the electronics.
